11 Virtual Team Meeting Games to Reconnect your Remote Team in 2022
Enter, virtual team meeting games. Fun activities in meetings are certainly nothing new, but we’re here to show you how to adapt team building games to the remote environment.
Bring Joy to your Meetings
Remote work can feel really remote for your team members. Virtual team meeting games help.
All the numbers really point to one thing: more and more online meetings in the future.
Help break the ice – Maybe your team is one that has only just formed, or maybe your meetings are pretty infrequent. If your team members are getting to know each other for the first time, or for the first time in a long time, virtual team meeting games are fantastic for breaking the ice.
Improved memory of meetings – Things that are different and fun are memorable, right?
The same thing goes for games in meetings. A team member who performs an activity that’s engaging and different from the norm is more likely to remember the details of your meeting afterwards.
Note that many of these games use AhaSlides, which is free software designed to connect users through interactive presentation, polling, and in this case, gaming.
Justin Timberlake’s one-season TV wonder, Spin the Wheel, would have been entirely unwatchable without the incredibly ostentatious, 40-foot tall spinning wheel in centre stage.
In your team meeting, spin for each player and give them a question depending on the amount of money they land on.
First to $1 million is the winner!
Productive meetings begin here. Try out our employee engagement software for free!
Before the activity begins, ask your staff for a few audio impressions of different staff members. If they’ve been working together for a long time, they’ve almost definitely picked up on some of the little innocent traits that their co-workers have.
Ask for 1 or 2-sentence impressions of different staff members. Keep it innocent and clean!
Add the correct answer along with any other accepted answers you think your team might propose.
Well, rummage through your phone’s photo library, gather them all, and give Picture Zoom a go.
Picture Zoom is great for reminding your co-workers that you are still a team with a wonderful shared history, even if it’s based on that ancient office printer that always prints stuff in green.
Write what the correct answer is, with a few other accepted answers as well.
In the quiz leaderboard slide that follows your type answer slide, set the background image as the full-sized image.
If you’ve ever played Balderdash, you might remember the ‘weird words’ category. This one gave participants a strange, but totally real word in the English language, and asked them to guess the meaning.
Simply ask them what the word means, let your team see everyone’s answer, then get them to vote for their favourites. This could either be the answer that sounds the most correct, or the funniest answer.
Get everyone to submit their ideas about what the word means.
Reveal the winner with the most votes.
Don’t let a global pandemic quash that bizarre, creative spirit in your team. Build a Storyline works perfectly to keep that artistic, weird energy of the workplace alive.
This is a virtual team meeting game that requires very little effort and runs behind the scene throughout the meeting. If you’ve got a smaller team, you can loop back around and get everyone to submit another sentence.
A great one for creativity, and some truly weird stories.
Add the ‘name’ box under ‘additional fields’ so you can keep track of who’s answered
Make sure the results are unhidden and presented in a grid, so the writers can see the story in a line before they add their part.
The level of competition they inspire and the hilarity that often ensues puts them squarely on the throne of engaging virtual team meeting games.
What’s more, it’s never been easier to download and play free quizzes with your staff…
Share the unique join code with your players to quiz them live!
Host’s view on desktop.
Need more quizzes for your virtual team meeting games?
Well, yeah, that’s totally mad, but in Household Movie, it’s also a winning entry!
For this, you can either let them choose the movie or give them one from the IMDb top 100. Give them 10 minutes, and once they’re done, get them to present them one by one and collect everyone’s votes on whose is their favourite.
Someone pitch The Tin Foil Lion King to Hollywood!
Give them 10 minutes to find whatever they can around their house that can recreate a famous scene from that movie.
Choose the layout of the results between a bar, donut or pie chart.
Hide the results until they’re all in and reveal them at the end.
If you never got one of those fake awards in high school for being the person with the highest probability of doing something that ended up being a woeful misjudgment of your character, now’s your chance!
In terms of virtual team meeting games with the best effort to hilarity ratio, Most Likely to… knocks them out the park. Simply name some ‘most likely’ scenarios, list out your participants’ names and get them to vote on who’s most likely.
Choose to hide the results and reveal them at the end.
If you’re unaware of the British game show Pointless, let me fill you in. It’s all based around the idea that more obscure answers to broad questions get more points, which is something you can recreate with AhaSlides.
For example, asking for ‘countries starting with B’ might bring you a bunch of Brazils and Belgiums, but it’s the Benins and Bruneis that will bring home the bacon.
Hide the results and reveal them at the end.
It’s your chance to create stunning artwork using nothing but the free tools on your computer. Except, by ‘stunning artwork’, we mean crudely drawn pixel replicas of beautiful masterpieces.
Of all our virtual team meeting games, this one probably requires the most effort on your part. You have to engage in some conditional formatting on Google Sheets and create a colour pixel map for each piece of artwork you want your team to recreate.
Under ‘Format rules’ select ‘Text is exactly’ and input the value of 1.
Repeat the entire process for a few different artworks (make sure the artworks are simple so that this doesn’t take forever).
Make a simple multiple choice slide on AhaSlides so that everyone can vote for their favourite 3 recreations.
We’ve mentioned the wonders of Drawful 2 before, but if you’re new to the software, it’s the best out there for some seriously out-the-box doodling.
Naturally, the quality of the pictures isn’t the highest, but the results are truly hysterical. It’s a great ice breaker for sure, but it’s also a virtual team meeting game that your staff will be begging to play again and again.
Open it up, start a new game and share your screen.
The rest is explained on the game. Have fun!
With that in mind, we advise using one virtual team meeting game in every meeting. Most of the time, games don’t go beyond 5 minutes, and the benefits they bring far outweigh any time you may consider “wasted”.
