Part of the point of team building activities in general is to get bums off seats and introduce a bit of mobility to the office or classroom. These 11 outdoor and indoor team building ideas are sure to get the energy flowing.
For this one, you can really think outside the box and try to unearth some truly interesting human facts amongst your players.
Create a human bingo card with attributes like ‘find someone who hates your favourite fruit‘.
Players go around and try to fill out their card by asking others about whether an attribute on the card applies to that person.
Once they have one, they must move onto the next person.
People who agree with the statement move to one side of the room, while people who disagree move to the other. People on the fence about it simply stay in the middle.
If there were any positives to take from 2020’s lockdown, one was certainly the creative ways in which people staved off the boredom.
Players choose any scene from that movie to act out, using props if they want.
Each person votes on their favourite re-enactment.
Place two members of each team on one line, then the other 2 players of each team on another line about 30 metres away.
Ever considered an egg and spoon race to be far too easy?
Well, that’s the premise of Minefield Egg Race, where blindfolded players navigate an obstacle course directed purely by their teammate.
Blindfold one player and give them an egg and spoon.
If they drop their egg or touch an obstacle, they have to start again.
Give the players at the back of their lines the same idiom.
When they have the idiom, that player turns back around, taps the shoulder of the person in front, and acts it out.
If Act out the Idiom is like back charades, then Back Drawing is essentially back pictionary.
Show all the player 1s the same image.
Player 2 tries to replicate the image on the board just from the feel on their back.
The aim, as it always should be in life, is to make the tallest freestanding tower of dried spaghetti that’s crowned by a marshmallow.
Put players into small teams.
When you shout Go, each team has 5-10 minutes to build the tallest tower.
This small group team building activity not only rewards teams with fliers that go the farthest or stay airborne the longest, but also the ones with premium aesthetic value.
Give each team 5 minutes to make 3 types of plane.
You’ll certainly find who your leaders are in Team Cup Stack. This one encourages constant communication, patience, perseverance and the fulfillment of a solid plan in a surprisingly difficult team task.
Put players into small teams of 5.
Indian Leg Wrestling is certainly best for students or younger employees, but really works for anyone who likes a bit of physicality in their team activities.
Have one player from each team leg wrestle with one player from every other team. Repeat until everyone has wrestled.
Top 4 teams play the semi-final and the final!
Not everyone is on board with full-action team-building activities. Sometimes it’s nice to slow it down with a brain teaser, in which teams have to tackle problems from different angles and come up with a solution.
Well take it from us, they’re much less annoying when you’re working on them as a team.
Give each group a series of matchstick puzzles to solve.
There are some truly magnificent logos out there, ones with exquisite hidden facets that you may not get at first glance.
Give each group a bunch of logos and tell them to find the hidden meanings of each.
Quickest to get all of them wins!
Seemingly that article is always a few degrees from separation from pretty much every topic in the universe.
Give each group two random items that seemingly have nothing to do with each other.
Each team reads their 6 degrees and you decide whether or not the connections are too tenuous!
