Over 90,000 presenting styles from over 90,000 speakers have been shown, and you probably have found yourself related to one of them. Whatever the style is, there are some common things among TED Talk presenters which you can keep in mind to improve your own performance!
You can also intertwine your stories into your talk to build up your opinion on the topic and present your argument persuasively. Apart from research-based evidence, you can use personal stories as a powerful tool to create a reliable, compelling presentation.
However interesting your speech may be, there may be times when the audience drift their attention away from your talk for a moment. That is why it is essential that you should have some activities that win back their attention and get them engaged.
For example, a simple way to do this is to make good questions relevant to your topic, which get them to think and work out an answer. This is a common way that TED speakers use to engage their audience!
You can also ask them to do small acts, like close their eyes and think about an idea, or an example relevant to the idea you are talking about, just like what Bruce Aylward did in his talk on “How We’ll Stop Polio for Good.”
