Bring the Joy of Festive Films !
If you want to make your own improvements to the quiz, you can change anything on the AhaSlides editor (make questions easier/harder and add questions, for example).
While the quiz is free to download and play, your audience size will be limited to 7 quiz players. For a one-time purchase of $2.95, you can increase the limit to 15 players, and for $6.95, you can increase it up to 30.
The Christmas movie quiz is made with AhaSlides, which is free live quizzing software that’s also great for polling. Let’s take a look at how any AhaSlides quiz works…
Your quiz players will get the following display on their phones. They all join the quiz via a unique code and can play from anywhere in the world with an internet connection.
The quiz player’s display is personal to them. It shows them the question and possible answers, lets them know if they got it right, and then reveals their overall point tally compared to other players.
We’ll leave them right here, underneath this virtual Christmas tree:
If you’re hosting your Christmas movie quiz online, then all of your quiz players will also need a laptop or desktop. This is in addition to their phones so that they can watch the screen sharing while you host.
Once you’re assured you’ve got the apparatus for the big day, you can begin changing your quiz in any way that you like. Here are a few ideas…
This Christmas movie quiz is solo by default, but you can easily change it into a team affair. Just navigate to the quiz editor by finding the ‘Christmas Movie Quiz’ on your dashboard, then follow the instructions below:
Click on ‘set team names’ and you’ll be able to write in the names for each of your teams. You can do this part on the day of the quiz, once the teams are settled and the names have been decided by the players.
When everything is set up and you’re ready to roll with your free Christmas movie quiz, it’s time to invite your players in. There are 2 really simple ways to do this:
Via the QR code, which is shown when you click on the top bar of a slide. Anyone can scan this unique barcode on their phone’s camera, after which they will be taken straight to the quiz.
Depending on your audience’s level of Christmas movie knowledge, some of the questions on this quiz might seem either like a breeze, or way too difficult. We’ve aimed for a mixture of difficulties to keep the playing field as even as possible, but if your family, friends or work colleagues are absolutely nuts for Christmas films, or absolute novices at Christmas films, there are always ways to change the difficulty.
Check out the instructions above for how to enable teamplay.
Get rid of the time pressure: As default, all questions have a 30-second time limit (45 seconds for the music round) and more points are awarded for faster answers. Lengthening the time limit and unchecking the checkbox for ‘faster answers get more points’ will remove the pressure to answer quickly and allow more time for thought.
Here’s a few ways you can alter this one for free:
