Mechanical injuries are mainly caused by the human body or part of the human body contacting the dangerous parts of the machine, or entering the dangerous area of the machine operation. The types of injuries include bruises, crushing injuries, rolling injuries and strangulation.
Rotating parts of mining machinery and equipment, such as shafts, wheels, etc., may entangle people’s clothing and hair and cause injuries. The protrusions on the rotating parts may injure the human body, or catch the clothing or hair of the person and cause injury.
