Generally, electronic scales should be calibrated with 1/2 or 1/3 of the full scale range. The standard calibration process is as below:
Balance with 1/100 tolerance and minimum scale 0.01g will use F1 weights to calibrate.
Calibration on corners: Choose weight in 1/3X value( X instead of weighbridge’s total capacity), put it on the four corners of the platform and weigh separately. The readout of four corners can’t out of allowable tolerance.
Linear calibration: Select 20% X and 60% X weights, place the standard weight in the center of the weigh scale countertop, weigh separately, and the reading should be compared with the standard weight. The deviation should not exceed the allowable error.
