Stainless steel weights have the characteristics of corrosion resistance, which reduces the error of the weights in the process of use. Then why stainless steel has the characteristics of more corrosion resistance?
As mentioned in the junior high school chemistry textbook, all metals react chemically with oxygen in the atmosphere to form an oxide film on the surface of the object. The oxide formed on the surface of ordinary carbon steel undergoes an oxidation reaction, and then the rust is amplified little by little, and finally a metal hole is formed.
