Although this came to mean the empty space that exists before 1 (and that later would become the limit between positive and negative numbers). But it was not considered to fill a digit as we use it in our Arabic script, as this writing system would come much later.
The numeral hieroglyphs can be read and translated into our Arabic numerals simply by inverting the above formula. If we see a number inscribed on a stone from Ancient Egypt, for example
It can be written both from left to right and vice versa, and vertically (top to bottom) as well.
