At first, he and his brother Epimetheus were entrusted with creating the animals and the human race. How to also provide everything necessary for them to live, both physical conditions and the habitat of each species.
It was at that moment that Prometheus was inspired by the creation of man with faculties different from those of animals. He made them thinking that they could fend for themselves, with reason and common sense in their actions.
It happened when Prometheus asked Zeus to allow his humans to have fire, so they could do many works and cook their food. However, Zeus refused to do so; which greatly annoyed Prometheus, so that in an oversight of the sun god, could draw some burning flame and take it to his beloved humans.
Until one good day, Hercules, who is passing through the area accompanied by a bow and arrow, sees the long-suffering titan and decide to release it without thinking twice. There is no doubt that Prometheus was infinitely grateful to Hercules for stopping to release him.
Once Prometheus is freed from eternal punishment, Zeus's thirst for vengeance relentlessly increases. Who could imagine what he would be able to do full of so much hatred and evil against the titan and all of humanity?
He met other very powerful gods and thus conspired in his next revenge. What would your next move be?
Hephaestus took part in this creation, who took clay and did all the physical parts, Athena made him all the clothes he wore, while Hermes dedicated himself to giving him femininity and sweetness in his treatment. Finally, Zeus was the one who gave her life and made the gift that she had for Prometheus.
The evils spread throughout the land without anyone being saved from them. In this Pandora's box it also contained hope, which did not escape along with the evils and misfortunes, because she closed it before it left.
Would you like to know a fantastic story of a flying horse, mythological characters and great adventures?
Spend an exciting time getting to know Pegasus, the horse with the wings, which made it very special in the Greek mythology. Here you will see how this equine is created in a mysterious way, it came to belong to one of the most powerful gods of Mount Olympus and why a beautiful constellation bears his name.
One of them is that it comes from the blood of Medusa and was created at the bottom of the sea, hence its name meant "Spring." Other is that Poseidon turned into a horse to be with Medusa and it was when she got pregnant.
This horse was characterized by having two amazing wings that allowed it to fly over Olympus, in the company of Zeus, the god of the Earth, who liked its abilities so much that he decided to take it over after knocking down Bellerophon, its old owner.
With his bad luck, the king's wife falls in love and does various tricks to win the sympathy of the unfortunate young man. As he did not get what he wanted, the evil queen lied about him, forcing her husband to remove him from the castle and send him to his father-in-law.
He is tasked with killing the fierce Chimera beast. In view of how difficult this assignment would be for Bellerophon, the goddess appears Atenea playing a very important role: gives him the golden bridle to tame Pegasus.
Unfortunately Bellerophon was filled with pride and wanted to be one more god. Zeus, totally annoyed by his daring, sent an insect to bite Pegasus.
This beautiful legend shows you the value of pets in all the adventures you can have in life. Pegasus can be any animal, and could form inseparable bonds with you and make the best team of companions in many unforgettable moments.
