3 How are Mayan numbers written?
Next we will list all the Mayan numbers from 1 to 1000. There are several images that you can download to your computer, mobile and even print to study them more in depth.
We hope this list is useful to you, you can download in PDF version by clicking here. If you have any questions with a number you can leave a comment at the end of this article.
Specialists consider that the Maya writing system are hieroglyphs, because it has a certain resemblance to the system used in Ancient Egypt. His writing was made up of a combination of ideograms and phonetic symbols, so it is quite difficult to decipher its content.
An interesting detail about the Mayan numbering system is that they invented it to measure time and not to do mathematical calculations. Thus, Mayan numbers have a direct connection to days, months and years, which is why the Mayan calendar is one of his best known works and is one of the most complete and accurate in the world.
At the bottom are the numerals (those that go from 0 to 20), while in the upper level the numbers are worth the numeral figure multiplied by 20.
The vigesimal system of the Mayans is considered one of the most accurate in the world. Likewise, it is believed that Mayan calendar is more accurate than the Gregorian calendar and that it even had the same precision as modern measurement systems.
Regarding geometry, it is known that Mayas were very clear about the concept of the triangle, square, rectangle, circle and circumference, plus they could measure angles. They knew a large number of geometric figures and geometric volumes, having the ability to measure and use them at their convenience.
In this numbering system the maximum number of divinities that could be represented was 14, so they were only enough to cover numbers from 0 to 13. What did you do to represent the 6 missing numbers up to 19?
Next we are going to see a very interesting video about the Mayan numbers:
Experts believe that the disappearance of the Mayan civilization took place between the XNUMXth and XNUMXth century of our era, which is one of the greatest mysteries in the history of mankind. Until today the reason for the progressive abandonment of the great Mayan cities, which had become huge cities with great cultural and technological advances, is unknown.
When the Spanish arrived in Yucatán in the XNUMXth century, the collapse of the Mayan civilization had occurred several centuries ago, so the contact of the Spaniards with the rest of the Mayan culture was not as important as the one it had with the Aztecs and other civilizations that still conserved large buildings.
The remains that remain for study and our knowledge are very scarce and extremely valuable.. Among the remains of Mayan knowledge, the Dresden Codex stands out, which is the oldest book in all of America, in which there is a whole section dedicated to the calendar and its numbering system.
