Olive oil is the natural oil extracted from olives. It is an essential part of the Mediterranean diet and has been cultivated in those regions for a long, long time.
Stroke is caused by a lack of blood supply to the brain - either due to a blood clot or bleeding. In developing countries, stroke is the second most common cause of death after heart disease.
A study with 841000 participants showed that olive oil was the only monounsaturated source of reduced risk of stroke and heart disease (1). Another research study involving 140000 participants concluded that those who had olive oil in their diet had significantly less chance of getting a stroke (2).
Especially combined with fish oil (full of Omega-3) it has been seen that olive oil can reduce rheumatism symptoms. A study that combined these two showed that participants in the study experienced significantly less joint pain, improved grip strength and less rigidity on the mornings (4).
Research has shown that olive oil can be preventive against diabetes (type 2 diabetes).Several research studies have shown that olive oil has a positive effect on controlling blood sugar levels and preventing insulin resistance (5).
Epidemiological studies have shown that people living by the Mediterranean have a lower risk of certain types of cancer - and many researchers believe that olive oil plays an essential role. The high content of antioxidants can reduce oxidative damage to cells caused by free radicals - which is believed to be one of the leading causes of the development of cancer (7).
In-vitro studies have shown that extra virgin olive oil can fight eight different strains of this bacterium - including three bacterial strains that are resistant to antibiotics (9). A human study showed that 30 grams of extra virgin olive oil daily for 2 weeks can fight up to 40% of Helicobacter pylori infections (10).
Alzheimer's disease is the most common neurodegenerative disease in the world. This is due to the gradual build-up of plaque inside the brain cells - which has been linked to high levels of pollution and exhaust exposure, among other things.
Large studies have shown that consuming olive oil in a Mediterranean diet reduces the chance of heart disease (1). Research has also shown that olive oil can lower the need for blood pressure regulating drugs by up to 48% (14).
It is important that you choose the right type of olive oil; namely extra virgin olive oil. This is unrefined, not mixed, not heat treated and thus still contains all the good nutrients.
Olive oil is probably the healthiest fat there is. These are eight incredibly exciting health benefits, all with the support of research (so you can argue above even the worst Besserwizzer you know!
