Why did I have so much back pain after pregnancy?
Having back pain, as well as the pelvis, after pregnancy is quite common due to all the changes that occur during and after pregnancy. The pain can come early or late in pregnancy, and also after the birth itself.
During pregnancy, changes occur as the abdomen grows. This in turn leads to weakened abdominal muscles which causes your posture to change, among other things you get an increased curve in the lower back and the pelvis / pelvis tips forward.
"Unfortunately, these changes do not go away overnight. Your back may continue to ache, before your muscles gradually regain their strength / function and your joints become less dysfunctional.
