If you want to know the price of industrial salt, you’ll have to be first.
Consumers are well aware of the transportation safety applications of industrial salt, from de-icing the wings of airliners to spreading a layer of brine on potentially icy roads.
Rock salt is needed to bring everything from detergent to contact solutions, and the companies that make these products need millions of tons of salt per year.
One of the advantages of buying in bulk is, of course, lower prices. The cost of manufacturing small packages and transporting industrial salt greatly increases the price of industrial salt purchased at the store.
For those with limited storage space, 500 kilograms of industrial salt will cost about half the cost of a full ton of salt. In either case, the total cost of purchasing a ton of salt is usually less than $100.
For those who are considering buying salt in bulk, a "modest increase" is easily achieved. Small businesses can easily purchase salt on a monthly, quarterly or yearly basis, depending on their personal overhead.
